WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.880
Identify priority workflows.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.080
This is actually a great opportunity to go
through

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.800
custom GPTs and choose to not migrate

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.180
ones that people don't use anymore

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.240
as a way to clean up your workspace.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.000
This is a great use case for

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.940
the ChatGPT admin plugin where you can
actually use

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.680
ChatGPT Work or Codex to

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.280
list all of the custom GPTs in your
workspace,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.680
their owners, and how many messages

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.400
have been sent in the last 30 days.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.520
This will give you a pretty good report of

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.440
which custom GPTs should be migrated more
urgently,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.720
and you can share this with your team to

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.200
help you prioritize.
